.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
.TH PKGMK 8 "" "imai #VERSION#" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
pkgmk \- build a CRUX software package
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pkgmk
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pkgmk
builds a package from Pkgfile in the current directory. It checks source files,
unpacks them, invokes build(), strips eligible outputs unless disabled,
creates an archive and checks its footprint. The resulting filename is
.IR name # version - release .pkg.tar. compression .
Source and package modification times determine whether a rebuild is needed.
.PP
The C executable drives option parsing and the build lifecycle through an
embedded Bash compatibility controller. Bash evaluates the Pkgfile and
executable configuration in a persistent context, preserving Bash arrays and
function overrides. Downloads, recipe execution and packaging use Bash
callbacks. Command-line options are parsed first, then
Pkgfile and the selected configuration are sourced in that order. Recipe or
configuration assignments can therefore override command-line settings.
These files are trusted executable code, not passive data. Root builds remain
supported and are not sandboxed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-install
Run pkgadd after a successful build.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-upgrade
Run pkgadd with its upgrade option after a successful build.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-recursive
Find Pkgfiles recursively and build each port. The recursive driver retains
legacy zero status even if an individual child build fails; inspect its output.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-download
Download missing remote sources.
.TP
.BR \-do ", " \-\-download-only
Download missing sources without building.
.TP
.BR \-eo ", " \-\-extract-only
Extract sources without building.
.TP
.BR \-utd ", " \-\-up-to-date
Only check whether the package is up to date.
.TP
.BR \-uf ", " \-\-update-footprint
Update .footprint from the last built package.
.TP
.BR \-if ", " \-\-ignore-footprint
Do not check the built package's footprint.
.TP
.BR \-in ", " \-\-ignore-new
Ignore added files when checking a footprint; missing or changed entries
still matter.
.TP
.BR \-um ", " \-\-update-md5sum
Update .md5sum using current sources.
.TP
.BR \-im ", " \-\-ignore-md5sum
Disable legacy MD5 checking.
.TP
.BR \-cm ", " \-\-check-md5sum
Check MD5 sums without building.
.TP
.BR \-us ", " \-\-update-signature
Update the port signature and SHA256 sums.
.TP
.BR \-cs ", " \-\-check-signature
Check the port signature and SHA256 sums without building.
.TP
.BR \-is ", " \-\-ignore-signature
Disable port signature checking.
.TP
.BR \-rs ", " \-\-refresh-signature
Sign existing checksums without regenerating them.
.TP
.BR \-sk ", " \-\-secret-key " " file
Use this signing key instead of /etc/ports/repository.sec, where repository
is the port directory's parent name.
.TP
.BR \-pk ", " \-\-public-key " " file
Use this verification key instead of /etc/ports/repository.pub.
.TP
.BR \-ns ", " \-\-no-strip
Do not strip executable binaries or libraries.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Build even when the package appears up to date.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-clean
Remove the built package and downloaded sources.
.TP
.BR \-kw ", " \-\-keep-work
Retain the temporary working directory.
.TP
.BR \-cf ", " \-\-config-file " " file
Read this configuration instead of /etc/pkgmk.conf.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the invoked command name, imai identity and version, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
Both dash and Bash are required, along with standard shell utilities and
mktemp. Archive creation and extraction use bsdtar with the selected codec.
MD5 and SHA256 generation normally use native digest operations. Source names
containing backslashes, newlines or carriage returns use md5sum or sha256sum
to retain the selected utility's filename encoding. Recipe digest calls with
options also use the external utility. Signing and verification use
.I /usr/bin/signify
when requested. Downloads use curl by default. Set PKGMK_DOWNLOAD_PROG to
wget for GNU-compatible wget or aria2c for aria2.
BusyBox wget is explicitly rejected. Additional options use PKGMK_CURL_OPTS,
PKGMK_WGET_OPTS or PKGMK_ARIA2_OPTS, respectively.
Aria2c defaults to 4 connections per server, 4 splits, a 20 MiB minimum split
size, 15-second connection timeout and 60-second timeout, with 3 attempts
and a 3-second retry delay. It does not load aria2.conf.
Failed downloads are never renamed to the final source filename.
Stripping uses file and binutils strip; manpage compression uses gzip.
Builds additionally need all tools invoked by the port.
BusyBox alone is not a complete build environment and does not supply all of
these specialized dependencies.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I Pkgfile
Trusted Bash package recipe; see pkgfile(5).
.TP
.I /etc/pkgmk.conf
Trusted Bash global configuration; see pkgmk.conf(5).
.TP
.I .footprint
Expected package inventory and metadata.
.TP
.I .md5sum
Legacy source checksums; MD5 does not establish authenticity.
.TP
.I .signature
Port signature and SHA256 sums. Port signatures are distinct from binary
package authentication; pkgadd accepts unsigned local packages.
.TP
.I .nostrip
Patterns selecting outputs not to strip.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The nonrecursive workflow uses these codes. Executable recipes or configuration
can explicitly exit with other statuses; Bash error handling also has its
normal conditional-command exceptions.
.TP
.B 0
Completed successfully, subject to the recursive-driver caveat above.
.TP
.B 1
General error, including footprint mismatch, build function failure and
installation via pkgadd failure, matching the legacy implementation.
A zero pkgadd status does not prove that every file was installed; see pkgadd(8).
.TP
.B 2
Invalid Pkgfile.
.TP
.B 3
Missing or inaccessible source, package or work directory.
.TP
.B 4
Source download failure.
.TP
.B 5
Source unpacking failure.
.TP
.B 6
MD5 mismatch.
.TP
.B 10
Signature or signature-checksum failure.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Broad recipe compatibility and full package-corpus coverage have not been
established. Do not run untrusted recipes or treat the work directory as a
security boundary.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkgfile (5),
.BR pkgmk.conf (5),
.BR pkgadd (8),
.BR pkginfo (8),
.BR pkgrm (8),
.BR rejmerge (8),
.BR bash (1),
.BR signify (1)
